  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Edge",
      "items": [
        "The ALB terminates TLS and routes by path: / to the frontend, /api/* to the backend",
        "An AWS WAF web ACL is attached to the ALB and starts in Count mode",
        "Services sit in private subnets; only the ALB is internet-facing"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "Runtime",
      "items": [
        "One reusable Terraform module builds two independent EKS clusters: backend and frontend",
        "The events service is a ClusterIP inside the backend cluster, so gRPC never crosses the ALB",
        "The browser only ever calls the Next origin: a server-side route handler proxies /api/* to the backend, so there is no CORS",
        "The frontend reaches the backend through a manual Endpoints/NodePort bridge, and images come from immutable ECR repos"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "violet",
      "title": "Single-owner data",
      "items": [
        "Two DynamoDB tables, one owner each: lives belongs to the backend, events-cache to the events service",
        "Each service has an IAM policy scoped to its own table only; neither can read the other",
        "A local emulator (Floci) runs the whole stack offline: Docker Compose, Terraform, then Kubernetes"
      ]
    }
  ]
}
